{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790379943,"nonce":"UKD7cwHL+2R43Dt5lX2HnNXr5cs=","title":"Calls through structurally typed receivers bind by bare method name or read a class instance as an anon","message":"Probe (scratch af/Main.hx):\n\n    typedef HasFetch = { function fetch():Int; }\n    typedef FnField = { fetch: () -\u003e Int };\n    class C { public function new() {} public function fetch():Int return 11; }\n    var a:FnField = { fetch: () -\u003e 7 };  a.fetch()      // prints 11 -- bound to C.fetch by NAME\n    var f = a.fetch; f()                                 // 7, correct\n    var c:HasFetch = new C();  c.fetch()                 // 11 (by-name luck)\n    var g = c.fetch; g()                                 // SIGSEGV: anon field read on a class instance\n\n`o.m(args)` with `o` anonymous-typed goes down the method path (resolve_function_typed_field only resolves CLASS receivers); MIR then binds `m` by bare name to any class/stdlib method of that name (`get` -\u003e Arc_get, `load` -\u003e Atomic_load, Issue10335) or drops the call when none exists. A function-typed field READ uses the anon-by-index path, which is wrong when the value is a class instance.\n\nBoth need a dispatch that works for anon objects AND class instances under a structural type (runtime lookup by field name), not a static binding. Blocks Issue10335; likely many Iterator/typedef-structural rows.","files":null}]}